WEBVTT

00:12:59.457 --> 00:13:03.514
it's like taking a very sudden
snapshot of the proton.

00:13:04.153 --> 00:13:05.308
What do you see?

00:13:05.332 --> 00:13:09.366
You see a frozen bunch of partons.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.572
They don't move,

00:13:10.596 --> 00:13:13.652
and because they don't move
during the course of the experiment,

00:13:13.676 --> 00:13:15.985
you don't have to worry
about how they're moving.

00:13:16.009 --> 00:13:18.615
You don't have to worry
about the forces between them.

00:13:18.639 --> 00:13:23.828
You just get to think of it
as a population of frozen partons."

00:13:24.314 --> 00:13:27.778
This was the key to analyzing
these experiments.

00:13:27.802 --> 00:13:30.576
Extremely effective.